    "created_at": "2023-02-24T22:46:53Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-02-24T22:46:53Z",
    "body": "You can change segment colors based on charge level like this (this is my current config):\r\n```toml\r\n[battery]\r\nfull_symbol = \"\\uF240 \"\r\ncharging_symbol = \"⚡️\\uF242 \"\r\ndischarging_symbol = \"\\uF242 \"\r\nunknown_symbol = \"\\uF241 \"\r\nempty_symbol = \"\\uF244 \"\r\ndisabled = false\r\nformat = '[ $symbol $percentage]($style) '\r\n\r\n[[battery.display]]\r\nthreshold = 10\r\nstyle = 'red'\r\ncharging_symbol = \"⚡️\\uF244 \"\r\ndischarging_symbol = \"\\uF244 \"\r\n\r\n[[battery.display]]\r\nthreshold = 30\r\nstyle = 'yellow'\r\ncharging_symbol = \"⚡️\\uF243 \"\r\ndischarging_symbol = \"\\uF243 \"\r\n\r\n[[battery.display]]\r\nthreshold = 60\r\nstyle = 'green'\r\ncharging_symbol = \"⚡️\\uF242 \"\r\ndischarging_symbol = \"\\uF242 \"\r\n\r\n[[battery.display]]\r\nthreshold = 80\r\nstyle = 'green'\r\ncharging_symbol = \"⚡️\\uF241 \"\r\ndischarging_symbol = \"\\uF241 \"\r\n\r\n[[battery.display]]\r\nthreshold = 100\r\nstyle = 'green'\r\ncharging_symbol = \"⚡️\\uF240 \"\r\ndischarging_symbol = \"\\uF240 \"\r\n```\r\n\r\nWhat I would like is to be able to control the style based on charging/discharging state as I can with [powerlevel10k](https://github.com/romkatv/powerlevel10k) (I'm currently moving from powerlevel10k to starship).",
